Where the public security organ traffic management department temporarily withholds or revokes a motor vehicle driver's license, it shall issue an administrative penalty decision letter.

Article 111: Administrative penalties of detention for violations of the provisions of this Law shall be adjudicated by county-level or city-level public security bureaus, public security branch bureaus, or public security organs equivalent to the county level.

Article 112: When the public security organ traffic management department detains a motor vehicle or non-motor vehicle, it shall issue a voucher on the spot and inform the party to go to the public security organ traffic management department to accept handling within the prescribed time limit.

The public security organ traffic management department shall properly keep the detained vehicle and shall not use it.

If the party fails to come to accept handling within the time limit and still fails to come to accept handling after being announced for three months, the detained vehicle shall be disposed of in accordance with the law.

Article 113: The period of temporary withholding of a motor vehicle driver's license shall be calculated from the date the penalty decision takes effect; if the motor vehicle driver's license is withheld before the penalty decision takes effect, one day of withholding shall offset one day of the temporary withholding period.

The period for reapplying for a motor vehicle driver's license after revocation shall be handled in accordance with the provisions on motor vehicle driver's license administration.

Article 114: The public security organ traffic management department may, based on traffic technical monitoring records, legally impose penalties on the owner or manager of a violating motor vehicle. Where the driver can be determined, penalties may be imposed in accordance with the provisions of this Law.

Article 115: Traffic police who commit any of the following acts shall be given administrative sanctions in accordance with the law:

(1) Issuing motor vehicle registration certificates, license plates, driving licenses, or inspection qualification marks to motor vehicles that do not meet statutory conditions;

(2) Approving motor vehicles that do not meet statutory conditions to install or use sirens, marker lights of police cars, fire engines, ambulances, or engineering rescue vehicles, or to spray paint marking patterns;

(3) Issuing motor vehicle driver's licenses to persons who do not meet the conditions for driving permission, have not taken the examination, or have failed the examination;

(4) Failing to implement the system of separation of fine decision and fine collection, or failing to turn over all fees legally collected, fines collected, and illegal income confiscated to the state treasury in accordance with regulations;

(5) Running or participating in running business activities such as driving schools or driving training classes, motor vehicle repair shops, or paid parking lots;

(6) Taking advantage of their position to accept property from others or seek other benefits;

(7) Illegally detaining vehicles, motor vehicle driving licenses, driver's licenses, or vehicle license plates;

(8) Using vehicles legally detained;

(9) Collecting fines on the spot without issuing a fine receipt or not truthfully filling in the fine amount;

(10) Engaging in favoritism and fraud, and unfairly handling traffic accidents;

(11) Intentionally making things difficult and delaying the handling of motor vehicle license plates and certificates;

(12) Using sirens and marker lights when not performing emergency tasks;

(13) Intercepting and inspecting normally traveling vehicles in violation of regulations;

(14) Stopping and boarding motor vehicles when not performing emergency official duties;

(15) Failing to perform statutory duties.

Where the public security organ traffic management department commits any of the acts listed in the preceding paragraph, corresponding administrative sanctions shall be given to the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons.

Article 116: Where administrative sanctions are given to traffic police in accordance with the provisions of Article 115 of this Law, their performance of duties may be suspended before the administrative sanction decision is made; if necessary, they may be placed in confinement.

Where traffic police are given administrative sanctions of demotion or removal from office in accordance with the provisions of Article 115 of this Law, they may be dismissed.

Where traffic police are given dismissal sanctions or are dismissed, their police ranks shall be cancelled; traffic police who are given administrative sanctions below removal from office shall have their police ranks lowered.

Article 117: Where traffic police use their authority to illegally possess public property, solicit or accept bribes, or abuse power or neglect duty, constituting a crime, criminal responsibility shall be investigated in accordance with the law.

Article 118: Where the public security organ traffic management department and its traffic police commit any of the acts listed in Article 115 of this Law, causing losses to the parties, they shall bear liability for compensation in accordance with the law.

Chapter 8 Supplementary Provisions

Article 119: The following terms used in this Law have the following meanings:

(1) "Road" refers to highways, urban roads, and places that are under the jurisdiction of a unit but allow social motor vehicles to pass, including squares, public parking lots, and other places used for public passage.

(2) "Vehicle" refers to motor vehicles and non-motor vehicles.

(3) "Motor vehicle" refers to wheeled vehicles driven or towed by power devices, traveling on roads, used for carrying passengers or goods, or for engineering special operations.

(4) "Non-motor vehicle" refers to traffic tools driven by human or animal power, traveling on roads, as well as traffic tools such as motorized wheelchairs for the disabled and electric bicycles that, although driven by power devices, have design maximum speed, empty vehicle weight, and external dimensions conforming to relevant national standards.

(5) "Traffic accident" refers to incidents causing personal injury or death or property loss due to fault or accident involving vehicles on roads.

Article 120: The license plates and certificates of in-service motor vehicles of the Chinese People's Liberation Army and the Chinese People's Armed Police Force, the inspection of in-service motor vehicles, and the assessment of motor vehicle drivers shall be the responsibility of relevant departments of the Chinese People's Liberation Army and the Chinese People's Armed Police Force.

Article 121: For tractors traveling on roads, the administrative management powers of the public security organ traffic management department prescribed in Articles 8, 9, 13, 19, and 23 of this Law shall be exercised by the competent departments of agriculture (agricultural machinery).

